    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-3-662-64106-4_5",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-3-662-64106-4_5",
      "title": "Societal Relevance of Geodetic Earth Observation",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Detlef Angermann, Roland Pail, ... Urs Hugentobler"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2022,
      "abstract": "High-precision satellite data provide valuable contributions for a wide range of tasks in our modern society. A fundamental geodetic product are global reference frames that ensure a uniform reference for all spatial data (geoinformation) worldwide. This is indispensable for all positioning tasks, satellite navigation and accurate cadastral, land and resource management. Precise satellite observations are also indispensable for reliably recording changes of our planet and thus generating important information on the Earth system. Geodetic observations provide the basis for determining the effects of climate change and for developing and operating warning systems to protect against natural hazards. Three topics of particular relevance to society are examined in detail: satellite navigation, Earth system research and climate change. With interview contributions from the renowned experts Günter Hein, Harald Lesch and Stefan Rahmstorf, the satellite-based view “from above” is significantly extended by their perspective “from outside”.",
      "abstract_not_available": false,
      "snippet": "High-precision satellite data provide valuable contributions for a wide range of tasks in our modern society. A fundamental geodetic product are...",
      "citationCount": 0,
      "openAccess_pdf": {},
      "url": "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-662-64106-4_5",
      "source": "Springer Nature Link",
      "rank": 6,
      "publicationTitle": "Mission Earth",
